WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.869
The drive into the
mountains is long and arduous.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:06.272
So Arde suggests we stop
for a bite along the way.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.509
Fortunately, in Sumatra,
street food is a way of life.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:13.012
On almost every corner, vendors
hock freshly made snacks from

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.648
pushcarts or
hole-in-the-wall shacks,

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:19.185
like this one selling bika,
a tea cake made from coconut.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.019
What is this?

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:20.987
Really good.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.055
It's everyone's favorite.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.056
Everyone's favorite.
Hello.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.124
- Hello.
- Hi.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:24.991
Nice to meet you.

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:26.159
My goodness.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.327
That incredible
smell, what is that?

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:28.795
They cook the cinnamon wood.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:29.629
Cinnamon wood.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.531
So this is bika.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.232
Bika.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:33.032
It's like a cookie, a--

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:33.867
Cake.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:34.667
Small cake.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.273
So it's almost like
an Indonesian macaroon.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.308
Well, pretty much like that.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.110
So that's a banana
leaf underneath there.

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.146
Yeah.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.280
Wow.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.082
And then see
how they close it.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.250
Oh, OK.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.185
Put the pot back
on, and it bakes it.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:53.153
Want to try?

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.621
OK.
Let me take that.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.255
OK.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.489
Thank you.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:57.323
Pew.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:00.360
Oh.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.494
No, no, no, no, no.
Here.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.629
Damn.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.798
It's like a bird [bleep]
all over my windscreen.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:05.632
Here we go.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:06.499
OK.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.600
Oh, no.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.868
[laughs]

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:09.936
Ah, yes.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:10.837
Oh.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.238
[bleep] Oh, I'm sorry.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.673
It hit the side of the pot.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.041
So can I have a look at
these ones that are cooked?

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.075
Let me get the tongs.
Here we go.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:16.943
[laughs]

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:17.844
Oh, sorry.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.912
[bleep]

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.213
See how they--

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.915
OK, got you.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.917
How many bika do you make a day?

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.918
[speaking indonesian]

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:25.752
2,000.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:26.586
2,000.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:27.554
2,000 bika.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.321
A week.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.856
- No, a day.
- A day.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:30.924
- Every day.
- Every day.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.791
Stop it, smartass.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:32.625
[laughs]

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:33.426
[laughs]

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.961
They make it look so easy.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:38.064
They're angling up to eight
beautiful biscuits in there.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.200
Now I couldn't even
get one, so yeah.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.202
I mean, practice makes
perfect, but how many

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.337
coconuts do you want to screw?

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.539
This is like typical
from this area only.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.741
And people normally
eat this while

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:51.911
having coffee in the afternoon,
like having a tea time.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:52.745
Mm-hmm.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.980
Mm-hmm.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.281
Excellent.
Thank you so much.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.483
- Thank you so much.
- [speaking indonesian]

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.383
- Oh, my lord.
- [speaking indonesian]

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.017
[speaking indonesian]

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.185
Yeah.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.186
My apology for
screwing so many up.

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:01.254
2,000 a day.

